# Line endings, pinned so every clone agrees (same rule as mass-measure-01/-02/-03, ratio-01).
#
# Without this the working tree depends on each machine's core.autocrlf (true on Windows Git),
# and deployments are copied from the working tree — so a CRLF checkout makes a package that
# cannot be reproduced from its own commit (verify-package.ps1 goes red on correct packages).
#
# State when added (2026-09-23, `git ls-files --eol`): 71 text files already LF in the index,
# 1 CRLF (translation/translation-screen-manifest.csv — renormalised in the same commit),
# 100 binary. The working tree was 72 × CRLF purely because of core.autocrlf=true.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary, so auto-detection is never the only thing protecting media and fonts.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pptx  binary
*.xlf   text eol=lf

# SVG is XML — text. "*.svg binary" would silently kill diffs on the illustrations.
*.svg   text eol=lf
